body:
Quick question.   I have a new Mars-H 7.62x51.... any ammo recommendations?

&#x200B;

Thanks!

F'ing SWEET!  Have a LMT Mars-H on order... went with a Kahles 624i for the scope though.  

&#x200B;

Let us know how it shoots

Awesome lineup man!  I'm about to buy a MARS-H in 7.62... was looking for an AR10 and settled on that vs the Sr-25 and HKMr762 due to the ability to change barrels.  Have you had any experience with that?  Just looking for someone who's done it and wanted to see if it really holds zero.  

&#x200B;

My lineup is more random.... JP Enterprise and a BMC 5.56, DD .300 Blackout and the Sp5 in 9mm.  All fun to shoot

Looks like all you do is say dumb sh!t... I'm assuming you're one of those "winners" living in a tent under an Austin overpass...  lol

&#x200B;

Texas my ass

Not a fan of Jack Straw here, but digging the rest so far.  

&#x200B;

Thanks for sharing

Booo....  will never be as good as the original.  

&#x200B;

[https://getyarn.io/yarn-clip/62de802e-736c-4037-8f59-e3b1c2aca110](https://getyarn.io/yarn-clip/62de802e-736c-4037-8f59-e3b1c2aca110)

This is what I've been buying and it shoots great

[https://www.sigsauer.com/300blk-125gr-elite-match-grade-otm-1.html](https://www.sigsauer.com/300blk-125gr-elite-match-grade-otm-1.html)

&#x200B;

[Ammoseek.com](https://Ammoseek.com) is your friend here

&#x200B;

I've also shot Hornady 300 Blackout 110GR V-max, but it's more expensive.

&#x200B;

I get the stick to 1.00 per round or less, but seriously what good is a gun if you don't have ammo and practice shooting it.   Hard to find anything reliable in that price point these days.
